    "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UDKi9MghXqWCN5EmgBpTG-zlFSyRgxAm/view": {
      "title": "3 Year CLTA Decision Sciences & MSBA",
      "description": "3 Year CLTA Decision Sciences & MSBA - Brampton Job Ad 26_27.pdf - Google Drive 3 Year CLTA Decision Sciences & MSBA - Brampton Job Ad 26_27.pdf File Download ⌘D Details D Print ⌘P View Show Thumbnail Outline Comments Hide comments Show comments Show all comments Zoom Fit 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 200% Insert Tools Find ⌘F Help Send feedback to Google Report abuse Keyboard shortcuts ⌘/ More Save changes Open with Sign in Page / 4 Download Print Zoom out Zoom in Hide file header Previous Next Hide thumbnails Hide navigation pane 1 2 3 4 Approve Reject View Details Request a review Learn more Signature pending Sign Reject View details Review Not Spam Remove forever Not Spam Loading… {\"id\": \"1UDKi9MghXqWCN5EmgBpTG-zlFSyRgxAm\", \"title\": \"3 Year CLTA Decision Sciences \\x26 MSBA - Brampton Job Ad 26_27.pdf\", \"mimeType\": \"application\\/pdf\"} Page 1 of 4 Algoma University is committed to undoing systemic and institutional discrimination and being publicly transparent and accountable. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are fundamental to our Special Mission. In keeping with the Seven Grandfather teachings that are the core values that inform our decisions as an institution, we are committed to creating a welcoming, inclusive, respectful, and safe environment where everyone belongs. These values, commitments, and practices are highlighted in our institutional strategies, including the Strategic Plan; Academic Plan; Research Plan, and EDI Plan. We live these values through the strength and richness that diversity brings to our workforce and welcome contributors from equity-deserving groups including Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, Persons with Disabilities, 2 Spirit, Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, and Queer persons. Algoma University (www.algomau.ca) is an innovative institution that embraces research, scholarship, and teaching to pursue its Special Mission. The Special Mission is founded upon cross-cultural learning between Indigenous and other communities within a spirit of healing and reconciliation. Algoma University’s five faculties — Business and Professional Studies, Computer Science and Technology, Cross-Cultural Studies, Humanities and Social Sciences, and Science — provide students with rich experiential learning opportunities across all of its campuses in Brampton, Sault Ste. Marie and Timmins. Algoma University works to enhance its research capacity through community engaged partnerships and ongoing development of graduate programming. We welcome those interested in this exciting time of growth! Algoma University has an existing vacancy in the position of: Job Title: Three (3) Year Limited Term Contract Appointment Assistant Professor in Decision Sciences Position Status: Temporary; OPSEU Local 685 Department: Department of Finance, Economics and Decision Sciences Location: Brampton, Ontario Preferred Start Date: May 1, 2027, or as negotiated Program and Faculty Context The Brampton expansion of the Master of Science in Business Analytics (MScBA) program increases the department's need for stable full-time faculty capacity in Decision Sciences and Business Analytics. Program relevant faculty responsibilities extend beyond classroom teaching to include student advising, capstone project supervision, curriculum development, and program Page 2 of 4 administration. The position will also contribute to undergraduate and other graduate programming requiring quantitative, analytical, or data-oriented expertise. Indigenization, Equity, Diversity and Inclusion The department’s programs actively support Algoma University’s commitments to equity, diversity, inclusion, internationalization, and its northern mandate by providing students from diverse academic, cultural, and professional backgrounds with opportunities to examine global economic issues and their impacts on communities, labor markets, businesses, and public policy. I-EDI perspectives arise naturally in areas such as global labor and migration, international economics, economic development, and global business strategy, where students are encouraged to examine how economic policies, institutions, and market forces affect different populations and regions. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to an inclusive learning and research environment and to demonstrate how principles of Indigenization, equity, diversity, and inclusion can inform their teaching, scholarship, mentorship, and service. Qualifications, Expectations & Application Process ● Qualifications ● Hold a Ph.D. in Decision Sciences, Management Science, Operations Research, Management Science, Business Analytics, Industrial Engineering, Data Analytics, or a closely related discipline. ● Candidates who are near completion of the Ph.D. may be considered provided that all degree requirements are completed before the appointment begins. ● Demonstrate a strong academic background and an active or emerging research program in a related field. ● Demonstrate the ability to teach graduate-level and undergraduate courses involving quantitative methods, analytics, modelling, and data-driven decision making. ● Demonstrate evidence of, or strong potential for, excellence in university teaching. ● Demonstrate the ability to supervise graduate students undertaking capstone projects, major research projects, or other applied research activities. ● Demonstrate the capacity to develop a productive program of research and pursue external or internal research funding. ● Demonstrate a commitment to collegiality, academic service, student mentorship, and curriculum and program development. Page 3 of 4 ● Demonstrate a commitment to Indigenization, equity, diversity, inclusion, and Algoma University's Special Mission. ● Expectations ● Teach graduate courses in the Master of Science in Business Analytics (MSBA) program and contribute to undergraduate teaching in Decision Sciences, Business Analytics, quantitative methods, and other related areas. ● Contribute to the development and delivery of courses in areas such as business analytics, quantitative decision making, optimization, management science, statistical modelling, and related analytical fields. ● Supervise MScBA students in capstone projects and other graduate research or applied-project components. ● Maintain an active research and scholarly program in Decision Sciences, Business Analytics, or a related field. ● Pursue appropriate opportunities for research funding, interdisciplinary collaboration, and engagement with external partners. ● Participate in curriculum development and the ongoing enhancement of the MScBA and related undergraduate and graduate programs. ● Mentor students and contribute to the academic and professional development of graduate and undergraduate learners. ● Participate actively in departmental, faculty, and university service. ● Undertake other responsibilities consistent with the OPSEU Local 685 Full-Time Faculty Collective Agreement. ● Application Packages shall contain the following: ● a cover letter outlining their suitability for the position; ● a current CV ● a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., examples of peer and/or student evaluations) ● a research statement or plan ● sample of relevant publications or scholarly work ● Indigenization, Equity, Diversity and Inclusion (I-EDI) statement ● Any additional materials required through the University’s recruitment process. ● Contact information of three referees will be requested of short-listed candidates Note: Application materials should be submitted as a single combined PDF file, with a file name that identifies the applicant. Details Comments General Info Type Dimensions Size Duration Location Modified Created Opened by me Sharing Description Could not preview the file There was a problem loading the details. Loading… Back Transcript Close side sheet Copy Add a comment Page 1 Page 1 of 4"
